===Etymology===
From {{af|en|Tupper|-ware|id2=substance, kind, or use}}. Named after {{w|Earl Tupper}}, who invented the product in 1942 and founded the company that produced it. Thus it is a genericised trademark.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|Tupperware|s}}

# A food-storage container (often plastic), or a set of such containers.
